12067	{"artifactId":"LLD-85e6a58693579b6d-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-85e6a58693579b6d-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:controller","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-01T12:14:54.418Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"n1","ref":"3.1","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"uxDefinitionToIr at src/workflow/artifacts/companion/ux.ts:275 returns DocumentIR and populates it with graph primitives — nodes.push at :288, a kind:'contains' edge at :289, and derived:{nodes,edges} at :299.","evidence":"CONFIRMED in substance with ONE line number off by one. ux.ts:275 is `export function uxDefinitionToIr(uxDef: UxDefinition): DocumentIR {`, :288 is `nodes.push({ id, label: labelFor(el), kind: el.type });` and :289 is the `kind: 'contains'` edge — all three verbatim. But :298 reads `scopeDescription: 'UX mock',`; the `derived: { nodes, edges },` line the LLD cites is at :299. I confirmed by reading :296-301 directly.","action":"Correct the LLD's `derived` anchor from ux.ts:298 to ux.ts:299. The PREMISE is unaffected — the return object does carry `derived: { nodes, edges }` and that is the whole load-bearing point — so this is a citation slip, not a design error. Worth fixing because a one-off anchor is exactly what erodes trust in a citation chain that is otherwise exact.","fixability":"auto","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The cited content exists and says what the LLD claims; only the line number is wrong by one, because :298 is the preceding scopeDescription field. A reader following the anchor lands one line short of the evidence.","artifactEdits":[{"find":"and derived:{nodes,edges} at :299","replace":"and derived:{nodes,edges} at :299"},{"find":"and returns them as `derived: { nodes, edges }` at :299","replace":"and returns them as `derived: { nodes, edges }` at :299"}]}},{"claimId":"n2","